---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/for/fashion';
const title = "Shopify cart recovery for fashion stores";
const desc = "Preserve the shopper\u2019s exact size and color, then resolve fit uncertainty.";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
<ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
<section class="container py-16 md:py-24">
<a class="link" href="/for">← All store types</a>
<h1 class="hero-title mt-6">Shopify cart recovery for fashion stores</h1>
<p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9">Preserve the shopper’s exact size and color, then resolve fit uncertainty.</p>
<article class="prose-shopify mt-12 max-w-4xl">
<h2>Recover the selected variant</h2>
<p>Treat a saved style without its size and color as an incomplete recovery record. Link to the selected variant and show the matching image. If that size becomes unavailable, stop urgency for that item; a back-in-stock invitation or an explicitly offered alternative is a different conversation. Do not silently replace the shopper’s choice.</p>
<h2>Resolve fit before choosing a promotion</h2>
<p>Use the relevant garment measurements, fit notes and actual exchange policy. Avoid universal claims that an item runs true to size. A message for a fit question should lead to that product’s guide; a release reminder should reflect actual availability. Keep drop waitlists, browse reminders and checkout recovery from sending competing offers to the same person.</p>
<h2>Proposed acceptance exercise</h2>
<p>Queue a two-item basket, sell out one size, then change the remaining color before opening the message. Inspect image, link, availability and discount scope. Complete a purchase in another session and inspect the queued follow-up. Compare a fit-help message against the existing message using completed orders and subsequent returns, with enough observation time for returns to appear.</p>
<h2>Select by variant controls</h2>
<p>Shortlist tools by demonstrated access to variant identifiers and pre-send inventory checks, not a generic Shopify integration badge. Require a preview of a partly unavailable basket and a record explaining why a shopper was excluded. Subtract discount, fulfillment and expected return handling from recovery contribution; a higher attributed order count can conceal expensive exchanges.</p>
<h2>Check the trigger before replacing the tool</h2>
<p>Shopify distinguishes checkout recovery from earlier cart activity. Review <a class="link" href="https://help.shopify.com/en/manual/promoting-marketing/create-marketing/abandoned-checkouts">Shopify’s recovery eligibility</a> and inspect the actual workflow before comparing replacements. Proposed exercises above have not been performed.</p>
<p>Related decisions: <a class="link" href="/for/digital-products">digital product shops</a> · <a class="link" href="/for/food-and-beverage">food and beverage brands</a>.</p>
</article>
</section>
</BaseLayout>
